The requested theorem has NOT been proved. Its scope is every complete nontrivially valued K and every actual good separated strict boundaryless PURE analytic curve, with finite continuous ordinary-zero-current h on an ordinary open U. After C=completion(algebraic closure K), it requires two uniformly decreasing ordinary CLD-smooth psh sequences approaching ±h_C on one compact strict affinoid inside each prescribed ordinary neighborhood, containing the point in its actual ordinary interior. Singularities, nilpotents, imperfect fields, positive characteristic and actual component Artinian lengths must remain.

The findings in n1 and n2 do not close the analytic gates. The indispensable obligations left unproved here are:
(1) completed-algebraic ordinary-current transport with exact compact-form descent, actual field embeddings, wild/Frobenius stages, componentwise purity and top-measure multiplicities;
(2) the reduction, normalization, conductor, continuous rigid-puncture and component-current chain, including unequal generic lengths, and any harmonic-normalization-to-ordinary-zero-current bridge;
(3) actual fixed-affinoid semistable formal-open and local finite-tree realization with the actual Shilov boundary, all analytic point types and prescribed ordinary-neighborhood constraints;
(4) simultaneous residual principal unit-log germs, every-direction slopes, whole annular collars and exact ordinary overlap gluing;
(5) assembly of both sequences on the same fixed compact affinoid.

Thuillier 2.3.8’s complete printed proof is accessible, including its asserted formal-open realization after boundary insertion. The required application has not been independently completed here. Lemma 2.2.22 distinguishes type-2 formal vertices from type-3 points on a skeleton. Residual exactness in 2.3.22 and the slope formula for already existing semistable unit charts in 2.2.25 do not provide this attempt with the missing simultaneous construction. Bosch–Lütkebohmert 7.1 concerns smooth geometrically connected PROJECTIVE curves. Wanner 1801.04713v3, Theorem 4.7, concerns algebraically closed smooth proper ALGEBRAIC curves and current positivity; it does not itself supply first-stage ordinary regularization. Algebraic tests are included in ordinary analytic tests, not conversely. Correct caps exclude positive-genus vertices, require a strict error margin and must be checked on whole annuli.

These are missing proofs, not counterexamples. No ordinary smooth harmonic approximation, psh gluing by partitions, G-cover-to-ordinary-open inference, total fibre-product purity, regular-element-to-S1 inference or non-strict-radius counterexample is used. Prior verdicts grant no theorem. General transcendental current ascent, downstairs all-K ordinary approximation and full original P06.2 remain unresolved. No strict analytic counterexample is constructed. P05.2 is untouched.

